## Context budget

Everything that enters context is re-sent on every later turn. Keep it small.

- **Search before reading.** `rg -l 'pattern'` to find files, `rg -n 'pattern' | head -n 30`
  to find lines. Read a whole file only when you genuinely need all of it.
- **Read ranges, not files.** Use `offset`/`limit`, or `sed -n '120,200p' FILE`.
  For structure first: `python3 <token-diet>/scripts/outline.py FILE`.
- **Bound every command.** Builds, installs and test runs get `2>&1 | tail -n 30`.
  `git log --oneline -n 20`. `git diff --stat` before any real diff. `curl -s ... | head -c 4000`.
- **Screenshots at `scale: 0.5`** unless small text must be read — image tokens scale with area.
- **Never re-read an unchanged file**, and never re-read a file to verify an edit.
- **Prefer a fresh session** over working near the auto-compaction threshold.
